From: qforge
Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: route the secondary touchscreen to the secondary output

Dual-screen boards have a digitizer on each panel. gamescope tied every
touchscreen on an I2C/SPI bus to "the" internal panel, so the bottom
panel's touches landed on the main output's window, scaled to its size.

--secondary-touch-device <input name> marks one touchscreen as the
secondary output's (matched on the libinput device name; on the AYN
Thor family the DTS label, e.g. bottom_touchscreen). Its touches are
rotated by that panel's orientation, scaled to the secondary output's
logical size (0041 sizes the window shown there to it) and always passed
through to that window's surface, which the compositor hands to wlserver
whenever the secondary focus or its surface changes, and wlserver drops
when the surface goes. They never move the pointer, warp the cursor or
change keyboard focus, so the game on the main output keeps its input,
and their ids are offset so the two digitizers never share one. Other
touchscreens keep the existing path untouched.

(qforge: dual-screen boards, step 5 of the dual-output plan, 2026-10-12.)
---
